  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 131 AM EDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nThis morning may hold the coldest lows of the forecast with \ntemperatures ranging from the low 30s over the higher terrain to \nupper 30s and low 40s for the central and southern valley. Winds \nhave calmed under surface high pressure, which will provide the ripe \nenvironment for frost development. Frost is likely for portions of \nthe northern plateau, Southern Appalachians, northeast TN, and \nsouthwest VA. \n\nSlight improvement in temperatures for this afternoon and frost \npotential into tomorrow morning, with increasing heights aloft \nfollowing the deep trough exiting to the east. Winds will be much \ncalmer compared to yesterday. Much of the coming week synoptically \ncan be characterized by omega blocking over the CONUS; troughing \nover the coasts and ridging in the middle of the country. Dry \nweather will continue through the rest of the forecast period with \ntemperatures eventually rising to a few degrees above normal.",
